      "swing_high": { "value": 1.21, "unit": "V", "source": { "closed_form": { "note": "p23 figure 5-46, section 5.12. The stroke center is 1.211 V below Vcc at 0.1 mA and 1.549 V below Vcc at 10 mA. The line through them falls 34.1 ohm and starts 1.208 V below Vcc, rounded to 1.21 V. The x-axis is printed Output Sink Current. The title is Output Sourcing Characteristics and the axis is the drop from Vcc, so the current is source current. The figure does not print a supply. Section 5.7's 5 V positive-rail row is a maximum of 1.5 V from V+ and has no typical" } } },
